Based on the second paragraph, why are platform companies not required to provide health insurance or paid leave to gig workers?', 'Because gig workers earn significantly higher hourly wages than traditional full-time employees.', 'Because labor unions have agreed to waive these rights in exchange for flexible working hours.', 'Because the platforms legally categorize their workers as independent contractors instead of employees.', 'Because government regulations strictly prohibit digital apps from offering retirement benefits.', 'Because gig workers only perform tasks on a temporary basis for less than a month.', 'C', 'Alasan Benar: Paragraf 2 menyatakan: "Because digital platforms typically classify these workers as independent contractors rather than formal employees, companies are legally exempt from providing standard labor protections."
Perbandingan Opsi Lain:
