How does Dr. Aris''s attitude in the first paragraph contrast with his attitude in the fourth paragraph?', 'He shifts from being dismissive of local advice to being receptive and collaborative.', 'He changes from being fearful of the ocean to becoming an expert deep-sea diver.', 'He moves from supporting traditional methods to relying exclusively on laboratory metrics.', 'He transitions from protecting marine life to prioritizing commercial harbor construction.', 'He goes from trusting Pak Tua completely to doubting the fisherman''s intentions.', 'A', 'He shifts from being dismissive of local advice to being receptive and collaborative.
