Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(B) Salah: Aris sejak awal adalah ahli biologi kelautan yang tidak takut laut.
(C) Salah: Arah perubahannya terbalik; ia justru meninggalkan ketergantungan mutlak pada metrik laboratorium.
(D) Salah: Tidak ada pembahasan mengenai pembangunan pelabuhan komersial.
(E) Salah: Awalnya ia tidak percaya, lalu di akhir cerita ia justru sangat mempercayai Pak Tua.
Passage 2: The Weaver of Kembang Goyang (Soshum)', true),
('e9b836b7-d8b7-5a3f-980f-500ae6b8a7b3', 'LBE', 126, '02. Theme, Main Idea, Moral, & Conclusion', 'Mudah', 'Passage 2 (Questions 6–10) — Tema: Soshum (Sosiologi & Sejarah Budaya)

The Weaver of Kembang Goyang

In a quiet neighborhood on the outskirts of Yogyakarta, Ibu Sari was the last artisan still practicing the intricate art of hand-drawn batik tulis using natural indigo dyes. While neighboring workshops had switched to mass-produced printed fabrics to satisfy fast-fashion tourists, Ibu Sari refused to compromise her months-long waxing and dyeing process. However, as bills piled up and young apprentices left for factory jobs in the city, she began to fear that her ancestral craft was doomed to fade into obscurity.

One afternoon, a young architecture student named Dimas visited her workshop while researching sustainable local materials. Fascinated by the geometric precision and botanical chemistry behind Ibu Sari’s patterns, Dimas realized that these motifs were not mere decorations; they were visual records of local philosophy and ecological balance. Yet, he noticed that Ibu Sari struggled to reach buyers who appreciated the cultural depth behind her work.

Instead of asking her to speed up production, Dimas offered to document the storytelling and mathematical symmetry of each cloth through a digital archive and an international exhibition. He paired every finished textile with a detailed narrative explaining the philosophical meaning of its motifs and the months of patience woven into its threads.

When the exhibition opened, collectors and designers were captivated by the authenticity of the pieces, eagerly purchasing the entire collection at fair, sustainable prices. Watching young visitors ask questions about the ancient symbols, Ibu Sari smiled with renewed purpose. She realized that preserving heritage did not require abandoning tradition for speed, but rather translating its timeless meaning for a new generation.

Source: Adapted from UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage Reports, "Safeguarding Traditional Batik Craftsmanship in Indonesia," 2022.

What is the main idea of the passage?', 'Mass-produced printed fabrics are destroying the economy of traditional villages in Yogyakarta.', 'A traditional batik artisan saves her dying craft by showcasing its cultural meaning to a modern audience with a student''s help.', 'Architecture students are better at designing traditional batik patterns than elderly artisans.', 'Natural indigo dyes are becoming too expensive to produce due to urban factory expansion.', 'International exhibitions are the only way for local artists to escape poverty in Indonesia.', 'B', 'A traditional batik artisan saves her dying craft by showcasing its cultural meaning to a modern audience with a student''s help.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Merangkum keseluruhan plot secara utuh: Ibu Sari yang hampir kehilangan pelanggannya (Paragraf 1) berhasil menyelamatkan seni batik tulisnya setelah Dimas membantu mengemas cerita filosofis di balik motifnya ke pameran modern (Paragraf 3–4).
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Hanya membahas masalah awal di Paragraf 1, tidak mencakup solusi di akhir cerita.
(C) Salah: Dimas tidak mendesain motif batik; ia mendokumentasikan filosofi dan narasinya.
(D) Salah: Teks tidak menyebutkan bahwa bahan pewarna indigo menjadi terlalu mahal.
(E) Salah: Kata "only way" terlalu mutlak dan tidak didukung teks.', true),
