Based on the first and second paragraphs, why was Ibu Sari''s craft initially at risk of disappearing?', 'Natural indigo plants had become completely extinct around Yogyakarta.', 'Local buyers preferred cheaper mass-produced alternatives, and younger workers sought factory jobs.', 'The government banned the use of traditional waxing tools in residential neighborhoods.', 'Dimas convinced her apprentices to abandon textile making for architecture school.', 'Her geometric patterns were too simple to attract any interest from visitors.', 'B', 'Local buyers preferred cheaper mass-produced alternatives, and younger workers sought factory jobs.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Disebutkan di Paragraf 1 bahwa bengkel lain beralih ke kain cetak massal untuk turis dan para pemuda magang pergi bekerja di pabrik kota.
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Tidak ada informasi mengenai kepunahan tanaman indigo.
(C) Salah: Tidak ada larangan pemerintah terkait alat membatik.
(D) Salah: Dimas datang belakangan untuk meneliti, bukan membujuk pekerja meninggalkan bengkel.
