What can be concluded from the third paragraph about the difference between "nudging" and "sludging"?', 'Nudging is used solely by private banks, whereas sludging is practiced exclusively by public schools.', 'Ethical nudging promotes individual well-being transparently, whereas sludging exploits cognitive biases for corporate gain.', 'Sludging is a beneficial policy tool that helps consumers cancel unwanted subscriptions easily.', 'Nudging requires strict government taxes, while sludging relies on voluntary donations.', 'There is no difference between the two concepts; both terms refer to illegal financial fraud.', 'B', 'Ethical nudging promotes individual well-being transparently, whereas sludging exploits cognitive biases for corporate gain.
