According to the first paragraph, how does "choice architecture" differ from traditional regulatory methods?', 'It relies on strict legal prohibitions and heavy financial penalties to force compliance.', 'It alters the presentation of options to guide behavior while preserving freedom of choice.', 'It assumes that all consumers possess perfect mathematical knowledge before buying products.', 'It eliminates all alternative options so individuals can only pick the government''s preferred choice.', 'It requires citizens to pass an economics exam before opening a savings account.', 'B', 'It alters the presentation of options to guide behavior while preserving freedom of choice.
