Which of the following best states the implied main idea of the second paragraph?', 'Plankton populations near the ocean surface are declining due to excessive feeding by deep-sea fish.', 'The nightly feeding habits of twilight-zone creatures serve as a vital natural mechanism for mitigating global warming.', 'Atmospheric carbon dioxide levels can only be reduced by artificially pumping gases into the deep sea.', 'Marine organisms produce toxic waste that accelerates temperature changes in deep ocean currents.', 'Surface-dwelling fish are more effective at trapping carbon than creatures living in the twilight zone.', 'B', 'The nightly feeding habits of twilight-zone creatures serve as a vital natural mechanism for mitigating global warming.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Paragraf 2 merinci bagaimana migrasi malam makhluk zona senja menyerap karbon dari permukaan ke laut dalam (biological carbon pump), sehingga mencegah suhu global naik lebih cepat.
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Teks tidak menyebutkan populasi plankton menurun drastis akibat dimakan.
(C) Salah: Kata "only" dan "artificially" salah karena teks membahas proses penyerapan karbon alami oleh makhluk hidup.
(D) Salah: Kotoran (waste) organisme tersebut justru membantu mengikat karbon di kedalaman, bukan mempercepat pemanasan.
(E) Salah: Teks tidak membandingkan efektivitas penyerapan karbon antara ikan permukaan dan ikan laut dalam.', true),
