Which statement best represents the implied main idea of the second paragraph?', 'Bone marrow transplants are no longer necessary for patients suffering from severe blood disorders.', 'Early clinical applications of CRISPR have successfully cured previously chronic genetic conditions in patients.', 'Laboratory-edited cells lose their effectiveness within a few months of being infused into the bloodstream.', 'Blood transfusions remain the safest long-term treatment for individuals with sickle cell anemia.', 'Physicians can now edit faulty genes directly inside a patient''s body without laboratory procedures.', 'B', 'Early clinical applications of CRISPR have successfully cured previously chronic genetic conditions in patients.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Paragraf 2 menyajikan bukti keberhasilan uji klinis CRISPR pada pasien kelainan darah parah yang sebelumnya butuh transfusi rutin, kini menjadi bebas gejala sepenuhnya.
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Terapi ini justru menggunakan sel punca sumsum tulang (bone marrow stem cells) pasien yang diedit dan dimasukkan kembali.
(C) Salah: Pasien tetap bebas gejala ("remained completely symptom-free"), tidak kehilangan efektivitasnya.
(D) Salah: Transfusi darah adalah metode lama sebelum adanya terapi gen CRISPR.
(E) Salah: Pengeditan gen dilakukan di laboratorium ("edited the faulty gene in a laboratory"), bukan langsung di dalam tubuh.', true),
('ac4d7266-e7ab-5dd8-86dd-fee698fc9a8f', 'LBE', 153, '03. Implied Main Idea (Gagasan Tersirat)', 'Sedang', 'Passage 3 (Questions 11–15) — Tema: Saintek (Bioteknologi & Rekayasa Genetika)

