What is the implied main idea of the third paragraph?', 'Cancer is an unavoidable side effect for every patient who undergoes somatic gene therapy.', 'Gene editing carries significant biological safety risks and profound ethical controversies regarding heritable changes.', 'International scientists have unanimously approved germline editing to eliminate all hereditary traits.', 'Somatic cell modifications are more dangerous to future generations than editing human embryos.', 'Off-target genetic mutations only occur when CRISPR is used on non-human organisms.', 'B', 'Gene editing carries significant biological safety risks and profound ethical controversies regarding heritable changes.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Paragraf 3 membahas dua tantangan utama CRISPR: risiko biologis berupa mutasi tak diinginkan (off-target effects/kanker) dan dilema etis terkait pengeditan sel nutfah (germline cells) yang diwariskan ke keturunan berikutnya (designer babies).
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Kanker adalah potensi risiko ("potentially triggering"), bukan kepastian bagi setiap pasien.
(C) Salah: Pengeditan sel nutfah masih memicu perdebatan global yang sengit, belum disetujui secara bulat.
(D) Salah: Pengeditan sel somatik hanya berdampak pada pasien individu, sedangkan sel nutfah/embrio berdampak lintas generasi.
(E) Salah: Off-target effects merupakan peringatan risiko dalam konteks terapi gen secara umum/manusia.', true),
