Based on the fourth paragraph, what is the primary focus of current regulatory efforts regarding CRISPR?', 'Banning all forms of genetic research in private university laboratories.', 'Permitting medical treatments for diseases while preventing cosmetic or non-therapeutic genetic enhancements.', 'Encouraging pharmaceutical firms to patent naturally occurring human DNA sequences.', 'Replacing international ethical committees with automated artificial intelligence systems.', 'Limiting access to gene-editing therapies exclusively to wealthy industrialized nations.', 'B', 'Permitting medical treatments for diseases while preventing cosmetic or non-therapeutic genetic enhancements.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Paragraf 4 secara eksplisit menyatakan bahwa badan regulator berupaya menetapkan batasan yang mendukung inovasi terapeutik penyelamat nyawa sekaligus melarang ketat peningkatan genetik non-medis ("strictly prohibiting non-medical genetic enhancements").
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Tidak ada upaya melarang seluruh riset genetika di universitas.
(C) Salah: Tidak ada pembahasan mengenai hak paten urutan DNA manusia.
(D) Salah: Teks tidak menyebut penggunaan kecerdasan buatan untuk menggantikan komite etik.
(E) Salah: Tidak ada pembatasan akses terapi berdasarkan kekayaan negara.
Passage 4: The 15-Minute City (Soshum)', true),
('c998b1a4-5ada-52b8-b4d3-502e7528b434', 'LBE', 156, '03. Implied Main Idea (Gagasan Tersirat)', 'Sulit', 'Passage 4 (Questions 16–20) — Tema: Soshum (Sosiologi Perkotaan & Tata Kota)

Throughout the twentieth century, urban planners across many rapidly growing cities designed infrastructure primarily around the private automobile. Wide multi-lane highways, sprawling suburbs, and vast parking lots became symbols of modern economic progress. However, this car-centric model has increasingly resulted in severe traffic congestion, hazardous air pollution, and fragmented neighborhoods where pedestrians feel unsafe and socially isolated.

In response to these urban challenges, cities from Paris to Seoul are embracing the "15-minute city" concept. Pioneered by urbanist Carlos Moreno, this model reimagines urban neighborhoods so that residents can access all essential daily needs—including workplaces, schools, grocery stores, healthcare, and parks—within a 15-minute walk or bike ride from their homes. By decentralizing urban services and reclaiming road space for bike lanes and pedestrian plazas, cities aim to reduce carbon emissions while revitalizing local community life.

The transition toward walkable, mixed-use neighborhoods also yields substantial economic and public health benefits. Studies show that pedestrian-friendly streets boost foot traffic and revenue for small local businesses compared to car-dominated avenues. At the same time, integrating active transportation into daily routines lowers rates of cardiovascular disease and obesity while fostering spontaneous social interactions among neighbors.

Nevertheless, implementing the 15-minute city requires careful attention to social equity. Without affordable housing policies, transforming neighborhoods into vibrant, walkable hubs can inadvertently drive up property values and displace low-income residents—a process known as green gentrification. True urban sustainability therefore depends on ensuring that accessible, livable neighborhoods remain inclusive for citizens of all socioeconomic backgrounds.

Source: Adapted from World Resources Institute (WRI) & C40 Cities Climate Leadership Group, "The 15-Minute City: Reimagining Urban Mobility and Equity," 2023.

What is the implied main idea of the first paragraph?', 'Suburban expansion has successfully eliminated traffic congestion in modern metropolitan areas.', 'Car-centric urban planning from the twentieth century has created serious environmental and social problems.', 'Private automobiles are the most efficient mode of transportation for densely populated cities.', 'Urban planners intentionally designed highways to prevent neighbors from interacting with one another.', 'Parking lots generate more economic revenue for cities than public parks or residential buildings.', 'B', 'Car-centric urban planning from the twentieth century has created serious environmental and social problems.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Paragraf 1 menguraikan bagaimana tata kota abad ke-20 yang berpusat pada mobil pribadi berujung pada kemacetan parah, polusi udara berbahaya, dan keterasingan sosial pejalan kaki.
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Ekspansi pinggiran kota (sprawling suburbs) justru memicu kemacetan parah, bukan menghilangkannya.
(C) Salah: Teks mengkritik ketergantungan pada mobil pribadi di perkotaan.
(D) Salah: Keterasingan sosial adalah dampak negatif yang tidak diinginkan, bukan tujuan desain jalan raya.
(E) Salah: Tidak ada perbandingan pendapatan antara lahan parkir dan taman kota.', true),
