What is the overarching implied main idea of the passage?', 'Replacing car-dependent infrastructure with walkable 15-minute neighborhoods offers major environmental, health, and economic gains, provided housing equity is protected.', 'Low-income residents benefit automatically whenever property values rise in newly renovated urban districts.', 'Twentieth-century highway systems should be expanded to accommodate the growing number of electric vehicles.', 'Green gentrification is an unavoidable consequence that makes urban sustainability impossible to achieve.', 'Urban planners must prioritize luxury real estate development to fund public bicycle infrastructure.', 'A', 'Replacing car-dependent infrastructure with walkable 15-minute neighborhoods offers major environmental, health, and economic gains, provided housing equity is protected.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Merangkum seluruh bacaan: masalah kota berbasis mobil (Paragraf 1), solusi dan manfaat lingkungan, ekonomi, serta kesehatan dari 15-minute city (Paragraf 2–3), dan syarat penting berupa perlindungan perumahan terjangkau agar tidak terjadi green gentrification (Paragraf 4).
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(B) Salah: Warga berpenghasilan rendah justru terancam tergusur jika harga properti naik tanpa kebijakan perumahan terjangkau.
(C) Salah: Teks menganjurkan pengurangan ketergantungan mobil, bukan perluasan jalan tol untuk mobil listrik.
(D) Salah: Green gentrification bisa dicegah dengan kebijakan perumahan terjangkau, bukan hal yang mustahil diatasi.
(E) Salah: Pembangunan properti mewah justru bertentangan dengan semangat inklusivitas sosial di Paragraf 4.', true),
('325de587-3d2b-5fb6-abcf-5dbdbc26b38b', 'LBE', 160, '03. Implied Main Idea (Gagasan Tersirat)', 'Sulit', 'Passage 4 (Questions 16–20) — Tema: Soshum (Sosiologi Perkotaan & Tata Kota)

Throughout the twentieth century, urban planners across many rapidly growing cities designed infrastructure primarily around the private automobile. Wide multi-lane highways, sprawling suburbs, and vast parking lots became symbols of modern economic progress. However, this car-centric model has increasingly resulted in severe traffic congestion, hazardous air pollution, and fragmented neighborhoods where pedestrians feel unsafe and socially isolated.

In response to these urban challenges, cities from Paris to Seoul are embracing the "15-minute city" concept. Pioneered by urbanist Carlos Moreno, this model reimagines urban neighborhoods so that residents can access all essential daily needs—including workplaces, schools, grocery stores, healthcare, and parks—within a 15-minute walk or bike ride from their homes. By decentralizing urban services and reclaiming road space for bike lanes and pedestrian plazas, cities aim to reduce carbon emissions while revitalizing local community life.

The transition toward walkable, mixed-use neighborhoods also yields substantial economic and public health benefits. Studies show that pedestrian-friendly streets boost foot traffic and revenue for small local businesses compared to car-dominated avenues. At the same time, integrating active transportation into daily routines lowers rates of cardiovascular disease and obesity while fostering spontaneous social interactions among neighbors.

Nevertheless, implementing the 15-minute city requires careful attention to social equity. Without affordable housing policies, transforming neighborhoods into vibrant, walkable hubs can inadvertently drive up property values and displace low-income residents—a process known as green gentrification. True urban sustainability therefore depends on ensuring that accessible, livable neighborhoods remain inclusive for citizens of all socioeconomic backgrounds.

Source: Adapted from World Resources Institute (WRI) & C40 Cities Climate Leadership Group, "The 15-Minute City: Reimagining Urban Mobility and Equity," 2023.

Based on the fourth paragraph, how can cities prevent "green gentrification" when adopting the 15-minute city model?', 'By halting all park renovations and bike lane construction in low-income districts.', 'By pairing urban infrastructure improvements with affordable housing protections.', 'By encouraging high-income residents to relocate exclusively to distant suburbs.', 'By increasing property taxes on small local businesses operating in walkable plazas.', 'By restricting access to public parks to long-term neighborhood homeowners.', 'B', 'By pairing urban infrastructure improvements with affordable housing protections.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Paragraf 4 menegaskan bahwa tanpa kebijakan perumahan terjangkau ("affordable housing policies"), perbaikan lingkungan dapat menggusur warga berpenghasilan rendah; sehingga keberlanjutan kota bergantung pada penjagaan inklusivitas perumahan bagi semua kelas sosial.
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Solusinya bukan menghentikan pembangunan taman/jalur sepeda, melainkan melindungi keterjangkauan hunian.
(C) Salah: Tidak ada anjuran memindahkan warga kaya ke pinggiran kota.
(D) Salah: Pajak bisnis kecil tidak dibahas sebagai solusi gentrifikasi.
(E) Salah: Membatasi akses taman hanya bagi pemilik rumah bertentangan dengan prinsip inklusivitas ruang publik.', true),
('c49e2a5d-92e1-50f3-8cb4-445714a3434e', 'LBE', 161, '04. Restatement & Paraphrasing (Part 1)', 'Mudah', 'Passage 1 (Questions 1–5) — Tema: Saintek (Biomimikri & Rekayasa Material)

For millions of years, living organisms have evolved intricate structural adaptations to survive in harsh environments. Today, engineers and material scientists are increasingly turning to "biomimicry"—the practice of emulating biological designs—to solve complex human engineering challenges. Rather than relying solely on energy-intensive manufacturing or toxic synthetic chemicals, researchers study how nature achieves remarkable strength, flexibility, and efficiency using minimal resources.

A prime example of biomimicry is inspired by the lotus leaf, which remains spotless even in muddy swamps. Under a microscope, the leaf''s surface is covered in microscopic wax-coated bumps that repel water droplets, causing them to roll off while picking up dirt particles along the way. By replicating this nanostructure on exterior paints and glass coatings, scientists have developed self-cleaning surfaces that dramatically reduce the need for chemical detergents and manual maintenance.

Another breakthrough stems from studying spider silk, a natural protein fiber that is five times stronger than steel by weight yet remarkably elastic. Attempting to manufacture synthetic equivalents traditionally required extreme heat and hazardous solvents, which often degraded the fiber''s strength. However, modern bioengineers have recently learned to mimic the spider''s natural spinning process at room temperature using water-based solutions, paving the way for biodegradable medical sutures and lightweight protective gear.

As sustainability becomes a global imperative, biomimicry offers a transformative paradigm shift in industrial design. Instead of viewing nature merely as a warehouse of raw materials to be extracted, modern innovators recognize ecosystems as a living library of proven blueprints. Embracing these time-tested biological strategies allows humanity to build resilient technologies that harmonize with, rather than deplete, the natural world.

Source: Adapted from AskNature (Biomimicry Institute) & MIT News, "Nature-Inspired Engineering and Sustainable Materials," 2023.

Which of the following best restates the sentence "Rather than relying solely on energy-intensive manufacturing or toxic synthetic chemicals, researchers study how nature achieves remarkable strength, flexibility, and efficiency using minimal resources." in the first paragraph?', 'Scientists avoid using natural resources because synthetic chemicals are more efficient and flexible for modern manufacturing.', 'Instead of depending exclusively on high-energy production and harmful artificial substances, researchers examine how nature creates strong, adaptable, and efficient structures with limited materials.', 'Energy-intensive factories are the only way for researchers to replicate the strength and flexibility found in biological organisms.', 'Researchers believe that nature wastes too many resources to achieve the strength required by modern synthetic engineering.', 'By combining toxic chemicals with minimal natural resources, scientists have eliminated the need for energy-intensive manufacturing.', 'B', 'Instead of depending exclusively on high-energy production and harmful artificial substances, researchers examine how nature creates strong, adaptable, and efficient structures with limited materials.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Opsi ini mempertahankan makna dan struktur pertentangan kalimat asli secara akurat melalui padanan kata: "Rather than relying solely" $\rightarrow$ "Instead of depending exclusively", "toxic synthetic chemicals" $\rightarrow$ "harmful artificial substances", dan "using minimal resources" $\rightarrow$ "with limited materials".
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Menyatakan ilmuwan menghindari sumber daya alam karena bahan sintetis lebih efisien (bertolak belakang dengan teks).
(C) Salah: Menyatakan pabrik boros energi adalah satu-satunya cara meniru alam (salah makna).
(D) Salah: Menuduh alam memboroskan sumber daya, padahal teks menyebut alam menggunakan sumber daya minimal.
(E) Salah: Teks menyatakan peneliti tidak bergantung pada bahan kimia beracun, bukan menggabungkannya.', true),
