Another way of saying the sentence "In the fourteenth century, the same trade routes that transported silk and spices inadvertently accelerated the westward spread of the bubonic plague, devastating populations across Asia and Europe." in the third paragraph is that...', 'During the 1300s, merchants intentionally used silk and spice routes to spread the bubonic plague to rival European cities.', 'In the 14th century, the commercial pathways used for luxury goods unintentionally sped up the transmission of the bubonic plague westward, causing massive fatalities in Asia and Europe.', 'The bubonic plague originated in Europe during the fourteenth century and completely halted the trade of spices in East Asia.', 'Populations across Asia and Europe were saved from the bubonic plague because merchants closed the trade routes in the 1300s.', 'Transporting silk and spices became more profitable in the fourteenth century despite minor outbreaks of disease along the routes.', 'B', 'In the 14th century, the commercial pathways used for luxury goods unintentionally sped up the transmission of the bubonic plague westward, causing massive fatalities in Asia and Europe.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: "inadvertently accelerated" $\rightarrow$ "unintentionally sped up", "westward spread of the bubonic plague" $\rightarrow$ "transmission of the bubonic plague westward", dan "devastating populations" $\rightarrow$ "causing massive fatalities".
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Penyebaran wabah terjadi secara tidak sengaja (inadvertently), bukan disengaja oleh pedagang.
(C) Salah: Wabah menyebar ke arah barat (westward) menuju Eropa, bukan berasal dari Eropa.
(D) Salah: Populasi di Asia dan Eropa justru hancur/terdampak parah (devastating), bukan terselamatkan.
(E) Salah: Wabah pes adalah bencana besar yang menghancurkan populasi, bukan sekadar wabah ringan.', true),
