Which of the following best restates the sentence "Furthermore, as maritime navigation technologies advanced in the fifteenth century, European powers sought direct sea routes to Asia to bypass overland middlemen, gradually diminishing the economic dominance of traditional Silk Road caravan cities." in the third paragraph?', 'Improvements in 15th-century sea navigation led European nations to pursue direct ocean paths to Asia to avoid land-based intermediaries, slowly weakening the commercial power of classic Silk Road trading hubs.', 'Traditional Silk Road caravan cities became wealthier in the fifteenth century by charging European powers higher taxes for maritime navigation.', 'Overland middlemen invented advanced maritime navigation technologies to help European powers reach Asia faster.', 'European powers abandoned direct sea routes in the fifteenth century because overland caravan cities offered cheaper prices.', 'The economic dominance of Silk Road cities ended overnight when European ships accidentally discovered the Mediterranean basin.', 'A', 'Improvements in 15th-century sea navigation led European nations to pursue direct ocean paths to Asia to avoid land-based intermediaries, slowly weakening the commercial power of classic Silk Road trading hubs.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Semua unsur kalimat terwakili: "maritime navigation technologies advanced" $\rightarrow$ "Improvements in 15th-century sea navigation", "bypass overland middlemen" $\rightarrow$ "avoid land-based intermediaries", dan "gradually diminishing the economic dominance" $\rightarrow$ "slowly weakening the commercial power".
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(B) Salah: Kota-kota karavan justru kehilangan dominasi ekonominya, bukan semakin kaya.
(C) Salah: Perantara darat (overland middlemen) adalah pihak yang ingin dilewati oleh bangsa Eropa, bukan penemu navigasi laut.
(D) Salah: Bangsa Eropa mencari jalur laut langsung untuk menghindari perantara darat, bukan meninggalkannya.
(E) Salah: Penurunan dominasi ekonomi terjadi secara bertahap (gradually), bukan dalam semalam.', true),
