Which of the following best restates the sentence "Studying its rise and transformation reminds modern societies that global connectivity brings immense cultural enrichment alongside complex systemic risks." in the fourth paragraph?', 'Analyzing the Silk Road''s history proves that modern globalization only produces systemic risks without any cultural benefits.', 'Examining the growth and evolution of the Silk Road teaches contemporary civilizations that worldwide interconnectedness yields great cultural value as well as intricate shared dangers.', 'Modern societies no longer face systemic risks from global connectivity because they have learned from the Silk Road''s transformation.', 'Cultural enrichment can only be achieved if modern societies isolate themselves from complex global trade networks.', 'The rise of the Silk Road demonstrates that systemic risks are easily avoided when nations focus exclusively on cultural exchange.', 'B', 'Examining the growth and evolution of the Silk Road teaches contemporary civilizations that worldwide interconnectedness yields great cultural value as well as intricate shared dangers.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: "Studying its rise and transformation" $\rightarrow$ "Examining the growth and evolution", "immense cultural enrichment" $\rightarrow$ "great cultural value", dan "complex systemic risks" $\rightarrow$ "intricate shared dangers".
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Konektivitas global membawa pengayaan budaya sekaligus risiko sistemik, bukan risiko saja.
(C) Salah: Masyarakat modern tetap menghadapi risiko sistemik dari konektivitas global.
(D) Salah: Teks tidak menganjurkan isolasi dari jaringan perdagangan global.
(E) Salah: Risiko sistemik tidak mudah dihindari begitu saja hanya dengan fokus pada pertukaran budaya.', true),
('ed8dc263-b204-586a-a8da-e1d8d313a93e', 'LBE', 181, '05. Drawing Conclusions & Logical Inference', 'Mudah', 'Passage 1 (Questions 1–5) — Tema: Saintek (Energi Terbarukan & Geologi)

Beneath the Earth''s crust lies an immense reservoir of thermal energy generated by the radioactive decay of minerals and residual heat from the planet''s formation. Unlike solar and wind power, which fluctuate depending on weather conditions and time of day, geothermal energy provides a continuous, reliable supply of baseload electricity. By drilling deep wells into underground reservoirs of hot water and steam, geothermal power plants can drive turbines twenty-four hours a day with minimal carbon emissions.

Historically, commercial geothermal energy was restricted to volcanically active regions along tectonic plate boundaries, such as Iceland, Indonesia, and parts of the western United States. In these areas, natural underground heat sits close to the surface, making extraction economically viable. However, regions without natural hydrothermal reservoirs were largely unable to tap into this clean energy source due to the prohibitive cost and technical difficulty of drilling through miles of solid granite.

Recent breakthroughs in Enhanced Geothermal Systems (EGS) are rapidly expanding the geographical potential of geothermal power. Borrowed from drilling techniques developed in the oil and gas industry, EGS involves injecting high-pressure fluid deep into hot, impermeable rock formations to create artificial fractures. Water is then circulated through these engineered cracks, absorbing heat before returning to the surface to generate electricity.

If EGS technologies continue to scale and decline in cost, geothermal power could transition from a niche regional resource into a cornerstone of global decarbonization. Because geothermal facilities require significantly smaller land footprints than massive solar farms or wind turbine arrays, they offer an efficient pathway for nations seeking to achieve net-zero emissions without sacrificing vast tracts of agricultural or natural land.

Source: Adapted from U.S. Department of Energy (DOE) & International Renewable Energy Agency (IRENA), "The Future of Enhanced Geothermal Systems," 2023.

What can be concluded from the first paragraph regarding geothermal energy compared to solar and wind power?', 'Geothermal energy produces higher carbon emissions than wind turbines during cloudy weather.', 'Geothermal energy offers greater consistency in power generation because it does not depend on atmospheric conditions.', 'Solar and wind power are completely incapable of generating electricity during daytime hours.', 'Geothermal power plants can only operate for a few hours each day to prevent mineral decay.', 'Radioactive decay inside the Earth''s crust makes geothermal electricity too dangerous for residential use.', 'B', 'Geothermal energy offers greater consistency in power generation because it does not depend on atmospheric conditions.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Paragraf 1 mengontraskan tenaga surya dan angin yang berfluktuasi mengikuti cuaca/waktu dengan energi panas bumi yang mampu memasok listrik beban dasar (baseload electricity) terus-menerus selama 24 jam tanpa terpengaruh kondisi atmosfer.
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Pembangkit panas bumi menghasilkan emisi karbon minimal (minimal carbon emissions), bukan lebih tinggi dari turbin angin.
(C) Salah: Tenaga surya justru bekerja optimal di siang hari; teks hanya menyebut outputnya berfluktuasi.
(D) Salah: Pembangkit panas bumi beroperasi 24 jam sehari, bukan beberapa jam saja.
(E) Salah: Peluruhan radioaktif alami di bawah kerak Bumi adalah sumber panasnya, bukan bahaya bagi rumah tangga.', true),
