What can be inferred from the second paragraph about how astronomers study exoplanet atmospheres?', 'They send robotic probes directly to distant stars to collect physical air samples.', 'They examine changes in starlight passing through a planet''s atmosphere during a transit to determine its chemical makeup.', 'They measure the gravitational pull of methane gas using radio antennas on the Moon.', 'They wait for exoplanets to collide with their host stars to observe the resulting chemical explosions.', 'They can only detect atmospheres on planets that completely block out 100 percent of their star''s light.', 'B', 'They examine changes in starlight passing through a planet''s atmosphere during a transit to determine its chemical makeup.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Paragraf 2 menjelaskan bahwa saat planet melintas di depan bintangnya (transit), astronom menganalisis cahaya bintang yang tersaring melewati atmosfer planet tersebut untuk mengidentifikasi jejak kimia gas seperti uap air, $CO_2$, dan metana.
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
