What can be concluded from the second paragraph about Pak Wayan''s initial proposal?', 'It prioritized financial profit and market efficiency over equal communal access to water.', 'It aimed to distribute free water to low-income farmers who could not afford cash crops.', 'It was immediately rejected by every single resident during the monthly village assembly.', 'It relied on ancient stone tablets to calculate a thirty percent increase in harvest revenue.', 'It proposed banning all cash crops to protect the village''s ancestral traditions.', 'A', 'It prioritized financial profit and market efficiency over equal communal access to water.
