Which overarching conclusion best summarizes the entire story?', 'Modern agribusiness spreadsheets are always more accurate than historical records kept by village elders.', 'Sustainable community development succeeds when modern economic strategies respect and preserve time-tested systems of social and ecological resilience.', 'Ancestral rules must never be questioned by younger generations returning from university.', 'Privatizing natural resources is the most reliable way to protect rural villages from climate change.', 'Traditional irrigation systems cannot survive without financial subsidies from urban markets.', 'B', 'Sustainable community development succeeds when modern economic strategies respect and preserve time-tested systems of social and ecological resilience.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Kesimpulan utama seluruh cerita: pembangunan ekonomi masyarakat yang berkelanjutan tercapai ketika strategi modern (pemasaran agribisnis) dipadukan dengan penghormatan terhadap tata kelola tradisional yang telah teruji menjaga ketahanan sosial dan ekologis (sistem air komunal).
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Spreadsheet modern terbukti memiliki celah karena hanya menghitung kondisi cuaca ideal dan mengabaikan pelajaran sejarah.
(C) Salah: Pertanyaan dan ide baru generasi muda tetap bermanfaat selama diselaraskan dengan kearifan lokal.
(D) Salah: Privatisasi sumber daya alam justru terbukti memicu konflik dan kerentanan saat krisis iklim/kekeringan melanda.
(E) Salah: Sistem irigasi tradisional Tenganan sudah bertahan mandiri selama berabad-abad tanpa subsidi pasar kota.', true),
('934f4500-87b5-5108-bff6-50aa9be63d0e', 'LBE', 201, '06. Advanced Restatement & Paraphrasing (Part 2)', 'Mudah', 'Passage 1 (Questions 1–5) — Tema: Saintek (Komputasi Kuantum & Keamanan Siber)

Classical computers, which power everything from smartphones to supercomputers, process information using binary bits that exist strictly as either a zero or a one. In contrast, quantum computers harness the principles of quantum mechanics to operate with "qubits," which can exist in multiple states simultaneously through a phenomenon known as superposition. This unique capability allows quantum processors to perform complex calculations exponentially faster than even the most advanced classical machines.

While quantum computing promises revolutionary breakthroughs in drug discovery, climate modeling, and financial optimization, it also poses an unprecedented threat to modern cybersecurity. Most current digital encryption methods rely on mathematical problems—such as factoring massive prime numbers—that would take classical computers thousands of years to crack. However, a sufficiently powerful quantum computer could solve these cryptographic puzzles in mere hours, potentially exposing sensitive banking records, medical files, and government communications.

To counter this impending vulnerability, cryptographers worldwide are racing to develop "post-quantum cryptography" (PQC). Unlike quantum key distribution, which requires specialized optical hardware, PQC consists of upgraded mathematical algorithms designed to run on existing classical infrastructure while remaining resistant to quantum attacks. Standardization agencies have already begun urging corporations and public institutions to inventory their encrypted data and initiate the transition toward quantum-resistant protocols.

Migrating global digital infrastructure to post-quantum security will undoubtedly be a complex, multi-year endeavor. Nevertheless, cybersecurity experts warn that delaying this transition could allow malicious actors to harvest encrypted data today with the intention of decrypting it once functional quantum computers become commercially available.

Source: Adapted from National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) & IBM Quantum Research, "Post-Quantum Cryptography and the Future of Cybersecurity," 2023.

Which of the following best restates the sentence "In contrast, quantum computers harness the principles of quantum mechanics to operate with ''qubits,'' which can exist in multiple states simultaneously through a phenomenon known as superposition." in the first paragraph?', 'Unlike classical machines, quantum computers utilize quantum physics laws to run on qubits capable of occupying several states at once via superposition.', 'Quantum computers avoid quantum mechanics principles so that qubits can remain strictly in a single binary state at any given time.', 'Superposition prevents quantum computers from using qubits to process multiple states simultaneously during complex calculations.', 'Classical computers and quantum computers both rely on superposition to switch rapidly between zeros and ones.', 'Qubits operate independently of quantum physics by limiting processors to one state per calculation cycle.', 'A', 'Unlike classical machines, quantum computers utilize quantum physics laws to run on qubits capable of occupying several states at once via superposition.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Memparafrasekan kontras dan istilah teknis secara presisi: "In contrast" $\rightarrow$ "Unlike classical machines", "harness the principles of quantum mechanics" $\rightarrow$ "utilize quantum physics laws", dan "exist in multiple states simultaneously" $\rightarrow$ "occupying several states at once".
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(B) Salah: Menyatakan komputer kuantum menghindari hukum mekanika kuantum dan hanya berada di satu keadaan biner (kontradiksi).
(C) Salah: Superposisi justru memungkinkan qubit berada dalam banyak keadaan sekaligus, bukan mencegahnya.
(D) Salah: Komputer klasik menggunakan bit biner (0 atau 1 secara terpisah), bukan superposisi.
(E) Salah: Qubit bekerja berdasarkan fisika kuantum, bukan terlepas darinya.', true),
('c030bfa0-6ff8-5990-9037-641f0ef0a39b', 'LBE', 202, '06. Advanced Restatement & Paraphrasing (Part 2)', 'Mudah', 'Passage 1 (Questions 1–5) — Tema: Saintek (Komputasi Kuantum & Keamanan Siber)

