Which of the following best restates the sentence "Most current digital encryption methods rely on mathematical problems—such as factoring massive prime numbers—that would take classical computers thousands of years to crack." in the second paragraph?', 'Modern digital encryption is easily broken by classical computers within a few hours using prime number factorization.', 'Today''s primary data protection techniques depend on complex math puzzles, like breaking down huge prime numbers, which standard computers would need millennia to solve.', 'Classical computers have already spent thousands of years solving the prime number problems behind modern cybersecurity.', 'Factoring massive prime numbers is an outdated mathematical method that no longer protects digital communications.', 'Digital encryption methods avoid mathematical problems because classical computers can crack them effortlessly.', 'B', 'Today''s primary data protection techniques depend on complex math puzzles, like breaking down huge prime numbers, which standard computers would need millennia to solve.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Padanan kata sangat tepat: "Most current digital encryption methods" $\rightarrow$ "Today''s primary data protection techniques", "factoring massive prime numbers" $\rightarrow$ "breaking down huge prime numbers", dan "thousands of years to crack" $\rightarrow$ "need millennia to solve".
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Komputer klasik butuh ribuan tahun untuk memecahkannya, bukan beberapa jam.
(C) Salah: Kalimat asli menggunakan bentuk pengandaian (would take), bukan fakta bahwa komputer klasik sudah bekerja selama ribuan tahun.
(D) Salah: Faktorisasi bilangan prima besar masih menjadi dasar metode enkripsi saat ini (current), belum usang.
(E) Salah: Enkripsi modern justru bergantung pada masalah matematika rumit tersebut.', true),
