Which of the following best restates the sentence "Rather than banning junk food or imposing higher prices on sugary treats, Pak Dimas proposed redesigning the cafeteria''s ''choice architecture''—a concept from behavioral economics known as nudging." in the second paragraph?', 'Pak Dimas recommended outlawing unhealthy snacks and taxing sugary foods instead of changing the cafeteria layout.', 'Instead of prohibiting unhealthy snacks or raising prices on sweets, Pak Dimas suggested reorganizing how options were presented in the cafeteria, a behavioral economics strategy called nudging.', 'Choice architecture involves increasing the price of nutritious meals so students are forced to buy sugary treats.', 'Pak Dimas argued that nudging only works when school administrators completely ban all junk food from campus.', 'Redesigning the cafeteria''s layout was rejected because behavioral economists prefer imposing strict taxes on sugary treats.', 'B', 'Instead of prohibiting unhealthy snacks or raising prices on sweets, Pak Dimas suggested reorganizing how options were presented in the cafeteria, a behavioral economics strategy called nudging.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: "Rather than banning junk food or imposing higher prices" $\rightarrow$ "Instead of prohibiting unhealthy snacks or raising prices", dan "redesigning the cafeteria''s ''choice architecture''" $\rightarrow$ "reorganizing how options were presented in the cafeteria".
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Terbalik; Pak Dimas justru menghindari pelarangan dan kenaikan harga/pajak.
(C) Salah: Choice architecture mengatur penempatan dan opsi bawaan, bukan menaikkan harga makanan bergizi.
(D) Salah: Nudging bekerja tanpa melarang (banning) makanan cepat saji.
(E) Salah: Usulan desain ulang tata letak diterima dan diterapkan oleh sekolah, bukan ditolak.', true),
