Another way of saying the sentence "He explained that human decision-making is heavily influenced by convenience, visual placement, and default options rather than purely rational calculation." in the second paragraph is that...', 'People make choices solely through careful, logical analysis without noticing where items are placed.', 'Human choices are shaped far more by ease of access, visibility, and preset selections than by strictly logical reasoning.', 'Visual placement and convenience have no impact on human decisions when default options are removed.', 'Rational calculation always overrides convenience whenever people choose food in a crowded cafeteria.', 'Default options force humans to make irrational decisions even when healthy food is hidden from view.', 'B', 'Human choices are shaped far more by ease of access, visibility, and preset selections than by strictly logical reasoning.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: "convenience, visual placement, and default options" diparafrasekan menjadi "ease of access, visibility, and preset selections", dan "rather than purely rational calculation" menjadi "than by strictly logical reasoning".
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
