Which of the following best restates the sentence "Crucially, students never felt their freedom of choice was restricted, because unhealthy snacks remained available for anyone willing to walk to the back counter to request them." in the third paragraph?', 'Students complained that their personal freedom was violated because unhealthy snacks were completely removed from the menu.', 'Importantly, students did not perceive any loss of autonomy since less nutritious treats were still accessible to those who made the effort to ask for them at the rear counter.', 'Unhealthy snacks were only sold to students who agreed to eat fresh fruit bowls near the cash register first.', 'Walking to the back counter was prohibited for students who wanted to purchase sugary pastries during lunch.', 'Students felt forced to choose bottled water because cashiers refused to sell pastries at the back counter.', 'B', 'Importantly, students did not perceive any loss of autonomy since less nutritious treats were still accessible to those who made the effort to ask for them at the rear counter.
