Which of the following best restates the sentence "By thoughtfully structuring everyday environments so that beneficial choices become the easiest ones, institutions can gently guide individuals toward healthier, more sustainable behaviors." in the fourth paragraph?', 'Organizations can subtly encourage people to adopt better, lasting habits by carefully designing daily surroundings so positive options are the most convenient.', 'Institutions must punish individuals who fail to make healthy choices in poorly structured everyday environments.', 'Beneficial choices are only possible when organizations remove all convenient options from daily life.', 'Gently guiding individuals toward healthier behaviors requires forcing them to ignore their everyday surroundings.', 'Sustainable behaviors cannot be achieved unless institutions constantly monitor every choice individuals make.', 'A', 'Organizations can subtly encourage people to adopt better, lasting habits by carefully designing daily surroundings so positive options are the most convenient.
