A balanced, diverse gut microbiome acts as a biological shield against chronic inflammation and metabolic disorders. When beneficial gut bacteria ferment soluble fiber from plant-based foods, they produce short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) such as butyrate, which nourish the cells lining the intestinal wall and strengthen the gut barrier. Conversely, diets dominated by ultra-processed foods, refined sugars, and low fiber starve these beneficial microbes, leading to a condition called "dysbiosis"—an imbalance linked to obesity, type 2 diabetes, and autoimmune conditions.

Furthermore, emerging neurobiological research has uncovered a bidirectional communication highway connecting the digestive tract and the central nervous system, known as the "gut-brain axis." Gut microbes produce neurotransmitters—including nearly ninety percent of the body''s serotonin—that influence mood, stress resilience, and cognitive clarity. Disruptions to microbial diversity can therefore manifest not only as digestive discomfort, but also as heightened anxiety and depressive symptoms.

Protecting this internal ecosystem requires deliberate lifestyle choices, particularly regarding diet and medication use. While antibiotics remain indispensable for treating severe bacterial infections, their indiscriminate overuse wipes out beneficial gut flora alongside harmful pathogens, underscoring the need for targeted medical prescriptions and fiber-rich nutrition.

Source: Adapted from Harvard T.H. Chan School of Public Health & Nature Reviews Microbiology, "The Human Gut Microbiome in Health and Disease," 2023.

Which of the following best restates the sentence "Conversely, diets dominated by ultra-processed foods, refined sugars, and low fiber starve these beneficial microbes, leading to a condition called ''dysbiosis''—an imbalance linked to obesity, type 2 diabetes, and autoimmune conditions." in the second paragraph?', 'Eating ultra-processed foods and refined sugars nourishes helpful gut bacteria and prevents metabolic illnesses like type 2 diabetes.', 'On the other hand, eating patterns heavy in heavily processed items and added sugars but lacking fiber deprive helpful bacteria of nutrients, triggering a microbial imbalance associated with obesity, diabetes, and autoimmune diseases.', 'Dysbiosis occurs when beneficial microbes consume too much soluble fiber, causing severe autoimmune conditions and weight gain.', 'Obesity and type 2 diabetes are exclusively caused by eating plant-based foods that starve the intestinal wall.', 'Refined sugars strengthen the gut barrier by preventing beneficial microbes from fermenting dietary fibers.', 'B', 'On the other hand, eating patterns heavy in heavily processed items and added sugars but lacking fiber deprive helpful bacteria of nutrients, triggering a microbial imbalance associated with obesity, diabetes, and autoimmune diseases.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Menjaga hubungan sebab-akibat dengan tepat: "ultra-processed foods, refined sugars, and low fiber starve these beneficial microbes" $\rightarrow$ "heavily processed items and added sugars but lacking fiber deprive helpful bacteria of nutrients", dan "an imbalance linked to..." $\rightarrow$ "a microbial imbalance associated with...".
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Makanan ultra-proses dan gula rafinasi membuat mikroba baik kelaparan, bukan memberi nutrisi.
(C) Salah: Dysbiosis dipicu oleh kekurangan serat dan kelebihan makanan olahan, bukan kelebihan konsumsi serat larut.
(D) Salah: Makanan nabati berserat justru menyehatkan dinding usus, bukan memicu obesitas dan diabetes.
(E) Salah: Serat larutlah yang difermentasi untuk memperkuat dinding usus, bukan gula rafinasi.', true),
