Another way of saying the sentence "Disruptions to microbial diversity can therefore manifest not only as digestive discomfort, but also as heightened anxiety and depressive symptoms." in the third paragraph is that...', 'Harm to gut bacteria variety affects only stomach comfort and has no connection to emotional or mental health.', 'An imbalanced gut microbiome can consequently appear not merely as stomach troubles, but also as increased anxiety and signs of depression.', 'Heightened anxiety and depression are the primary causes of improved microbial diversity in the digestive tract.', 'Digestive discomfort prevents gut microbes from producing the serotonin needed to eliminate all forms of anxiety.', 'Maintaining microbial diversity guarantees that individuals will never experience digestive discomfort or depressive symptoms.', 'B', 'An imbalanced gut microbiome can consequently appear not merely as stomach troubles, but also as increased anxiety and signs of depression.
