Which of the following best restates the overarching message of the first and second paragraphs combined?', 'Historically, doctors correctly believed that all bacteria in the human gastrointestinal tract must be eradicated to prevent chronic inflammation.', 'Modern DNA research shows that a fiber-fed gut microbiome actively supports immunity and intestinal health, whereas low-fiber processed diets cause harmful microbial imbalances.', 'Short-chain fatty acids like butyrate are ultra-processed chemicals that damage the cells lining the intestinal wall.', 'Human cells synthesize ninety percent of dietary fibers without any assistance from gastrointestinal microorganisms.', 'Autoimmune conditions can be cured overnight simply by avoiding all plant-based foods and soluble fibers.', 'B', 'Modern DNA research shows that a fiber-fed gut microbiome actively supports immunity and intestinal health, whereas low-fiber processed diets cause harmful microbial imbalances.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Merangkum inti Paragraf 1 (pengurutan DNA mengungkap peran aktif mikrobioma usus dalam imun dan pencernaan serat) dan Paragraf 2 (serat menyehatkan dinding usus, sedangkan makanan olahan rendah serat memicu dysbiosis).
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Anggapan lama dokter bahwa semua bakteri harus dibasmi telah dibantah oleh riset DNA modern.
(C) Salah: Asam lemak rantai pendek (butirat) adalah senyawa alami hasil fermentasi serat yang menyehatkan usus, bukan bahan kimia olahan berbahaya.
(D) Salah: Mikrobioma usus memproduksi hampir 90% serotonin tubuh (Paragraf 3), bukan sel manusia memproduksi 90% serat pangan.
(E) Salah: Makanan nabati dan serat larut justru penting untuk mencegah ketidakseimbangan mikroba, bukan dihindari.
Passage 4: Digital Conservation of Cave Art (Soshum)', true),
('11d30ed4-3656-5595-8205-46a7ceac74d7', 'LBE', 216, '06. Advanced Restatement & Paraphrasing (Part 2)', 'Sulit', 'Passage 4 (Questions 16–20) — Tema: Soshum (Arkeologi & Konservasi Budaya Digital)

Preserving the Fading Murals of Goa Leang-Leang

Deep inside the limestone karst caves of Maros-Pangkep in South Sulawesi, prehistoric hand stencils and dynamic hunting scenes painted over forty-five thousand years ago adorn the cavern walls. For millennia, these ancient rock art panels survived undisturbed in the stable microclimate of the caves. Recently, however, archaeologist Dr. Hendra and his conservation team documented an alarming acceleration in surface exfoliation, where mineral crusts blister and flake away due to rising temperatures and extreme seasonal humidity linked to climate change.

Realizing that physical restoration alone could not halt the geological weathering of the limestone walls, Dr. Hendra initiated an urgent digital preservation project. Using high-resolution laser scanning and photogrammetry, his team captured sub-millimeter three-dimensional models of every cave chamber and pigment layer. These digital twins record not only the exact geometry and color spectrum of the artwork, but also microscopic tool marks left by Paleolithic artists.

Beyond safeguarding the murals against physical loss, the three-dimensional archive has democratized access to cultural heritage. Previously, strict conservation rules limited cave entry to a handful of researchers to prevent human breath and body heat from accelerating wall decay. Now, students, scholars, and global museum visitors can explore interactive virtual reconstructions of the caves without placing fragile prehistoric surfaces at risk.

Reflecting on the mission, Dr. Hendra emphasized that digital conservation is not a substitute for protecting physical heritage sites, but rather an essential insurance policy. By pairing climate adaptation strategies on the ground with meticulous digital documentation, humanity can ensure that its earliest artistic expressions endure for future generations.

Source: Adapted from Aubert, M. et al., Nature ("Pleistocene Cave Art in Sulawesi") & UNESCO World Heritage Centre Digital Conservation Reports, 2023.

Which of the following best restates the sentence "Recently, however, archaeologist Dr. Hendra and his conservation team documented an alarming acceleration in surface exfoliation, where mineral crusts blister and flake away due to rising temperatures and extreme seasonal humidity linked to climate change." in the first paragraph?', 'Lately, Dr. Hendra''s team recorded a worrying speedup in rock surface peeling, caused by climate-driven heat and severe seasonal moisture changes.', 'Dr. Hendra discovered that rising temperatures and seasonal humidity help stabilize mineral crusts on ancient cave walls.', 'Surface exfoliation has slowed down recently because climate change eliminated extreme humidity inside the limestone caves.', 'Archaeologists recently painted new hunting scenes over the blistering mineral crusts to protect the cave walls from heat.', 'For millennia, extreme seasonal humidity prevented prehistoric hand stencils from surviving inside the Maros-Pangkep caves.', 'A', 'Lately, Dr. Hendra''s team recorded a worrying speedup in rock surface peeling, caused by climate-driven heat and severe seasonal moisture changes.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: "alarming acceleration in surface exfoliation, where mineral crusts blister and flake away" diparafrasekan menjadi "worrying speedup in rock surface peeling", dan "rising temperatures and extreme seasonal humidity linked to climate change" menjadi "climate-driven heat and severe seasonal moisture changes".
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(B) Salah: Kenaikan suhu dan kelembapan ekstrem justru merusak dan mengelupaskan kerak mineral, bukan menstabilkannya.
(C) Salah: Pengelupasan permukaan justru semakin cepat (acceleration), bukan melambat.
(D) Salah: Tim arkeolog mendokumentasikan kerusakan, bukan melukis adegan berburu baru di atas dinding gua.
(E) Salah: Lukisan prasejarah bertahan selama ribuan tahun berkat iklim mikro gua yang stabil sebelum perubahan iklim terjadi.', true),
