Another way of saying the sentence "Previously, strict conservation rules limited cave entry to a handful of researchers to prevent human breath and body heat from accelerating wall decay." in the third paragraph is that...', 'In the past, tight preservation regulations restricted cave access to only a few scientists so that visitor breathing and warmth would not speed up rock deterioration.', 'Conservation rules previously encouraged thousands of tourists to enter the caves daily to keep the walls warm.', 'Human breath and body heat were proven to protect prehistoric cave walls from decaying under strict regulations.', 'A handful of researchers previously banned all conservation rules so they could study the caves without restrictions.', 'Wall decay accelerated in the past because conservation rules failed to limit the number of researchers entering the caves.', 'A', 'In the past, tight preservation regulations restricted cave access to only a few scientists so that visitor breathing and warmth would not speed up rock deterioration.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: "strict conservation rules limited cave entry to a handful of researchers" $\rightarrow$ "tight preservation regulations restricted cave access to only a few scientists", dan "prevent human breath and body heat from accelerating wall decay" $\rightarrow$ "so that visitor breathing and warmth would not speed up rock deterioration".
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(B) Salah: Aturan konservasi justru membatasi masuknya pengunjung, bukan mengundang ribuan turis.
(C) Salah: Napas dan panas tubuh manusia mempercepat pelapukan dinding gua, bukan melindunginya.
(D) Salah: Tidak ada peneliti yang membatalkan aturan konservasi tersebut.
(E) Salah: Aturan konservasi berhasil membatasi akses peneliti demi mencegah percepatan kerusakan akibat napas dan panas tubuh.', true),
