Based on the third paragraph, what underlying assumption does the author hold about healthy urban communities?', 'Healthy communities require complete silence in all public parks and libraries.', 'Strong civic life depends on citizens tolerating everyday unpredictability and remaining attentive to one another in shared spaces.', 'Individual comfort is far more important than collective presence in modern cities.', 'Digital technology is the only reliable way to build empathy among strangers.', 'Urban neighborhoods function best when residents avoid interacting with people from diverse backgrounds.', 'B', 'Strong civic life depends on citizens tolerating everyday unpredictability and remaining attentive to one another in shared spaces.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Pada Paragraf 3, penulis berasumsi bahwa komunitas nyata memang bising, tak terduga, dan beragam, sehingga menjaga keutuhan masyarakat menuntut kesabaran, perhatian terhadap sekitar, dan kehadiran kolektif (collective presence).
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(A) Salah: Penulis justru menyatakan dunia nyata secara alami tidak sunyi (inherently noisy), dan memaksakan keheningan digital merusak interaksi sosial.
(C) Salah: Penulis mengkritik kecenderungan memprioritaskan kenyamanan individu di atas kehadiran kolektif.
(D) Salah: Teknologi digital dalam konteks ini justru dituding membangun "dinding sosial tak terlihat", bukan membangun empati.
(E) Salah: Penulis justru menghargai keberagaman (diverse) dan interaksi spontan antarwarga.', true),
