What makes the statement "company revenue increased by an average of 1.4 percent compared to previous periods" in the first paragraph a fact?', 'It reflects the personal belief of labor union leaders.', 'It is an objective, quantifiable measurement recorded during the empirical study.', 'It predicts what will happen to global corporations over the next decade.', 'It uses value-laden adjectives to judge the morality of corporate profits.', 'It represents a government mandate enforced by British parliament.', 'B', 'It is an objective, quantifiable measurement recorded during the empirical study.
