According to the third paragraph, all of the following statements about mycelium composites are TRUE, EXCEPT:', 'They can be grown using agricultural byproducts such as corn stalks and sawdust.', 'They serve as eco-friendly replacements for conventional leather and synthetic packaging.', 'They take several decades to break down naturally when buried in garden soil.', 'Their manufacturing process requires very low energy inputs.', 'Material scientists consider them vital components of a circular bioeconomy.', 'C', 'They take several decades to break down naturally when buried in garden soil.
