Passage 3: Dissolving Microneedle Patches (Saintek)', true),
('59180815-5266-50de-a173-36fb3fac968d', 'LBE', 411, '16. Stated & Unstated Information', 'Sedang', 'Passage 3 (Questions 11–15) — Tema: Saintek (Ilmu Material & Teknologi Kesehatan)

Traditional pharmaceutical injections rely on hypodermic needles that pierce deep into skin tissue, causing pain, triggering needle phobia in roughly 20 percent of adults, and generating billions of hazardous sharps that require specialized biohazard disposal. Moreover, most liquid vaccines must be stored and transported within strict cold-chain refrigeration networks, creating major logistical hurdles in rural or low-income regions with unreliable electricity.

To overcome these limitations, biomedical engineers have developed "dissolving microneedle patches"—small adhesive squares lined with hundreds of microscopic, cone-shaped needles made from water-soluble polymers or sugars. Measuring less than one millimeter in length, these tiny projections painlessly penetrate only the outermost layer of the skin (the stratum corneum) without reaching deeper pain receptors or blood vessels.

Once applied to the skin like a standard bandage, the microneedles dissolve within minutes upon contact with interstitial fluid, releasing encapsulated vaccine antigens directly into the epidermis—a tissue densely populated with specialized immune cells known as Langerhans cells. Clinical trials indicate that delivering vaccines directly to these skin-resident immune cells can generate robust antibody responses using a fraction of the standard liquid dose.

Because the dried vaccine formulation inside the polymer matrix remains stable at ambient room temperatures for months, microneedle patches eliminate the need for expensive refrigeration and trained medical personnel. Health organizations anticipate that self-administered microneedle patches could dramatically accelerate global immunization campaigns during future pandemics.

(Source: Adapted from Nature Biomedical Engineering & World Health Organization (WHO) Innovation Reports, "Dissolving Microneedle Patches for Pain-Free Immunization," 2024)

Which of the following is STATED in the first paragraph about conventional hypodermic needles?', 'They are completely painless for all adult patients.', 'They trigger needle phobia in approximately 20 percent of adults and create hazardous biohazard waste.', 'They allow liquid vaccines to be stored safely at warm room temperatures without refrigeration.', 'They never require trained medical professionals to administer injections.', 'They dissolve naturally inside the skin within minutes after injection.', 'B', 'They trigger needle phobia in approximately 20 percent of adults and create hazardous biohazard waste.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Tersurat secara eksplisit pada kalimat pertama Paragraf 1: "...triggering needle phobia in roughly 20 percent of adults, and generating billions of hazardous sharps that require specialized biohazard disposal."
