In the second paragraph, why does the author contrast "reconstructive" with "reproductive"?', 'To clarify that remembering is an active process of rebuilding fragments susceptible to alteration, rather than replaying an exact copy.', 'To argue that biological reproduction is controlled by cognitive psychologists.', 'To show that digital files are easier to corrupt than human brain cells.', 'To prove that leading questions have no impact once an event has been stored in memory.', 'To explain why post-event suggestions only affect children rather than adults.', 'A', 'To clarify that remembering is an active process of rebuilding fragments susceptible to alteration, rather than replaying an exact copy.
Alasan Jawaban Benar: Pada kalimat pertama Paragraf 2 ("human memory is fundamentally reconstructive rather than reproductive"), pengontrasan kedua istilah tersebut berfungsi meluruskan cara kerja otak: mengingat bukanlah memutar ulang salinan persis (reproductive), melainkan merakit kembali kepingan ingatan (reconstructive) yang rentan berubah oleh informasi baru.
Perbandingan dengan Opsi Lain:
(B), (C), (D), dan (E) Salah: Tidak membahas reproduksi biologis makhluk hidup; tidak membandingkan kerusakan berkas digital dengan sel otak; pertanyaan mengarahkan terbukti memengaruhi ingatan; dan efek misinformasi berlaku pada manusia secara umum (termasuk peserta dewasa dalam eksperimen).', true)
